    "body": "## What changes\n\nSkill is still `1 + log_score / R`, but the reference `R` is no longer the uniform guess. It is now the crowd marginal a participant can compute in each phase:\n\n- **Phase 1**: per-item option shares of the `TRAIN` rows, scored on `DEV`.\n- **Phase 2**: per-item option shares of the `TRAIN` + `DEV` rows, scored on `TEST`.\n\n```\nm_j[k] = (visible count of option k on item j + 0.5) / sum over options\nm~_j   = floor + (1 - K_j * floor) * m_j\nR      = -(mean over held-out cells of log m~_j[truth])\nskill  = 1 + log_score / R\n```\n\nThis is exactly the predictor in `baseline/marginal_counts`, so that baseline scores 0 in both phases. 1 is still perfect; a uniform guess is now well below 0.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `R` depends on the data and differs between phases. It was a schema-only constant before.\n- The phase-1 Laplace scale divides by the new `R`, which is smaller than the uniform reference, so the noise is somewhat larger. `R` is treated as a fixed constant of the release; the `privatize` docstring says what that leaves unaccounted.\n- `score.py`: `marginal_reference()` added, `uniform_reference()` removed, `score()` takes the reference as an argument, and the log key is `marginal_reference`.\n- README, the `config.yml` leaderboard comment, and the six tutorials are updated. The tutorial's crowd-baseline cell now prints skill `0.0000`.\n\n## Needs a native-speaker check\n\nThe reworded tutorial strings in `fr`, `es`, `ru`, `zh` and `ar` (`k_and_gates`, `score_intro`, `lbl_skill_note`, `lbl_reference` in `tutorials/translations.yml`).\n\n## Verification\n\n`score.py --submission baseline/marginal_counts` on fresh sandboxes, un-noised skill from the organizer log:\n\n| Instrument | Phase | skill | marginal_reference |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| sample | 1 | 0.0 | 0.892454 |\n| sample | 2 | 0.0 | 0.909499 |\n| unicef | 1 | 0.0 | 1.308458 |\n| unicef | 2 | 0.0 | 1.318744 |\n| world_bank | 1 | 0.0 | 1.536594 |\n| world_bank | 2 | 0.0 | 1.529349 |\n\nAll six notebooks were rebuilt with `tutorials/build.py --force` and re-executed; outputs other than the scoring cell are unchanged.",
