    "body": "Native-speaker proofread of the Russian tutorial. All changes were made in the `ru` block of `tutorials/translations.yml`, with `tutorials/ru.ipynb` regenerated via `python tutorials/build.py` after each pass (unchanged cells keep their outputs; no other language is touched).\n\n**Scope: the full notebook** — every key in the `ru` pack was reviewed against the English original.\n\nMain kinds of changes:\n- **Naturalness**: reworded sentences that read as literal translations (e.g. the class-system and gate-logic paragraphs, the section-2 intro, the bad-model discussion).\n- **Terminology**: consistent survey-methodology vocabulary — «оцениваемая совокупность», «основа выборки», «опросные инструменты», «интервью» (for interviews/fieldwork), «условие перехода» (gate). \"Prediction-powered inference\" is kept in English where the concept is introduced.\n- **Precision fixes**: restored details lost in translation (census roster, \"whether anyone has a phone\"), replaced «наты» with «(при натуральном логарифме)», clarified that `score.py` reads roles but never splits.\n- **Table labels and printed strings** (`lbl_*`, `col_*`, `role_*`, docstrings) tightened for grammar; printf placeholders (`%.0f %%`, `%d`) preserved.\n- **Formatting conventions preserved**: backticks on identifiers in markdown cells, plain text in code comments/docstrings (matching the English convention), original bold/italic emphasis carried over.\n\nOne deliberate small departure from the English: in the gate-logic paragraph the \"free points\" sentence is replaced with an explicit instruction that the model should put its probability on `NA_GATED` for determinable cells.",
